From 66682696f688f7450ea5cb2a9da73e918c5a63bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:00:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] navi-vaults: add fees and revenue for NAVI's vaults on Sui

One listing for NAVI's navi_vault product, covering all four production
vaults (USDC and SUI, in NAVI's Prime and High Yield product lines).
Prime vs High Yield is off-chain product labelling over a single
contract, so it is one adapter; the fetch sums every vault group the
endpoint reports, so a group added later needs no adapter change.

Decomposition follows fees/AGENTS.md: a management fee is charged on
assets rather than carved out of the interest, so fees = yield +
management fee, revenue = management fee + performance fee, supply side
= yield - performance fee. The adapter rejects a payload where the
performance fee exceeds the yield, which is what keeps supply-side
revenue non-negative without allowNegativeValue. Fee amounts come from
NAVI's accounting; no rate is hardcoded or assumed.

version 1 because the endpoint only serves whole-UTC-day aggregates
keyed on fromTimestamp, so hourly windows are not available.

Marked doublecounted: the vaults earn by supplying into NAVI's own
lending markets and fees/navi already books 100% of that borrower
interest as its dailyFees, so reporting the same yield here would count
it twice in chain and category totals. The flag is adapter-wide, so it
also keeps the new management and performance fee revenue out of those
totals; counting nothing twice was preferred.

`start` is omitted rather than guessed: the endpoint does not serve the
vaults section for any date yet, so no date can be named as the earliest
that actually returns data.

NAVI_DEFILLAMA_CF_PASS is added to ENV_KEYS so getEnv resolves it. No
DEFAULTS entry: the value is not committed, it goes to maintainers out
of band, so the adapter test is expected to fail in PR CI until it is
set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
